{id:"D001",symbol:"Eucl",type:"family, indexed by k∈ℕ, of Euclidean metric spaces",definition:"Eucl(k)=ℝ^k, the real coordinate vectors indexed by {0,...,k−1}, with distance dist(x,y)=(∑_{j<k}(x_j−y_j)^2)^(1/2). Eucl(0) consists of the empty vector. On Eucl(k)×ℝ we use dist((x,t),(y,u))=(dist(x,y)^2+|t−u|^2)^(1/2), identified with Eucl(k+1) by appending the last coordinate; no maximum product metric is used. Balls mean {y:dist(x,y)<a}. All these spaces carry the topology of this metric and its Borel measurable structure.",depends_on:[],requires:[],binders:[{symbol:"k",type:"natural number"}],objects:["k"]},
{id:"D002",symbol:"diam",type:"extended nonnegative diameter of a subset of a metric space",definition:"For a subset A of a metric space X, diam(A)=sup{dist(x,y):x,y∈A} in [0,∞], with sup∅=0. Thus diam∅=0. When diam(A)≤a<∞ we treat it as the corresponding finite nonnegative real number. Countable sums of nonnegative quantities mean the supremum of finite partial sums, and may be infinite; powers with positive exponent have 0^s=0 and ∞^s=∞.",depends_on:[],requires:[],binders:[{symbol:"X",type:"metric space"},{symbol:"A",type:"subset of X"},{symbol:"x",type:"point of X"},{symbol:"y",type:"point of X"},{symbol:"a",type:"nonnegative real number"},{symbol:"s",type:"positive real exponent"}],objects:["X","A","x","y","a","s"]},
{id:"D003",symbol:"H",type:"Hausdorff content and measure functions on Euclidean sets with positive real exponent",definition:"For every k∈ℕ, A⊆Eucl(k), s>0 and δ>0, H^s_δ(A)=inf{∑_{i≥0}(diam U_i)^s : (U_i) is a countable cover of A and diam U_i≤δ for every i}, and H^s(A)=sup_{δ>0} H^s_δ(A), with values in [0,∞]. Finite covers are allowed by padding with empty sets; empty members contribute zero. The infimum of an empty collection is ∞. This is exactly the unnormalized diameter-power convention of problem.md:34–42.",depends_on:["D001","D002"],requires:[],binders:[{symbol:"k",type:"natural number"},{symbol:"A",type:"subset of Eucl(k)"},{symbol:"s",type:"positive real number"},{symbol:"δ",type:"positive real scale"},{symbol:"U",type:"sequence of subsets of Eucl(k)"}],objects:["k","A","s","δ","U","Eucl","diam"]},
{id:"D004",symbol:"Native",type:"pair of native Hausdorff measure and dimension constructions on an extended metric space",definition:"For an extended metric space X with its Borel measurable structure, Native(X).measure(σ) denotes MeasureTheory.Measure.hausdorffMeasure σ, defined in the pinned library as Measure.mkMetric(r↦r^σ). Here mkMetric forms, for each positive extended radius, the covering outer measure with cost r^σ of the extended diameter for nonempty sets (empty sets cost zero), and takes their supremum as the radius decreases to zero, with the Borel measure structure. Evaluations on arbitrary sets mean outer measure evaluations, without requiring those sets measurable. Extended powers use the native ENNReal.rpow convention, including r^0=1. Native(X).dimension(A) denotes dimH A, defined as sup over a∈[0,∞) with Native(X).measure(a)(A)=∞ of the extended nonnegative number a; an empty supremum is zero. This names the exact native definitions, not an assertion about H.",depends_on:["D002"],requires:[],binders:[{symbol:"X",type:"extended metric space with its Borel measurable structure"},{symbol:"σ",type:"real exponent"},{symbol:"r",type:"extended nonnegative real number"},{symbol:"A",type:"subset of X"},{symbol:"a",type:"nonnegative real number"}],objects:["X","σ","r","A","a","diam"]},
{id:"D005",symbol:"dim_H",type:"extended nonnegative Hausdorff dimension of Euclidean sets",definition:"For k∈ℕ and A⊆Eucl(k), dim_H(A)=Native(Eucl(k)).dimension(A), the usual Hausdorff dimension, valued in [0,∞]. In particular the empty set has dimension zero by this definition. No finiteness is imposed by this definition; finiteness of the dimensions occurring in the target is proved below.",depends_on:["D001","D004"],requires:[],binders:[{symbol:"k",type:"natural number"},{symbol:"A",type:"subset of Eucl(k)"}],objects:["k","A","Eucl","Native"]},
{id:"D006",symbol:"I",type:"subset of ℝ",definition:"I=[0,1]={t∈ℝ:0≤t≤1}.",depends_on:[],requires:[],binders:[{symbol:"t",type:"real number"}],objects:["t"]},
